  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3.5. Increased capacity of member States to formulate and implement labour market programmes and employment services for transitions to decent work over the life course, with particular focus on young and older workers</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Directorate General of TVET/Ministry of Labour and Vocational Training in Cambodia adopted the plan to integrate gender-responsive employment services in TVET institutions. With this, all public TVET institutions in Cambodia will be able to enhance their existing career counselling and job placement services in their institutions.

The Public Employment Service delivery process has been strengthened through digitalization of employment services design and delivery as well as strengthening of partnerships with employers&apos; and workers&apos; organizations and other key stakeholders. The ILO, through ILO/SDC &quot;Decent Employment for Youth in Cambodia&quot; and ILO/China &quot;Strengthening Skill Development in Cambodia, Lao, and Myanmar through South-South and Triangular Cooperation&quot; projects, supports the Directorate General of TVET/ Ministry of Labour and Vocational Training to pioneer the process towards the integration of the gender-responsive employment services into public TVET services. ILO support includes: (1) Consultation with Directors of all public TVET institutions in Cambodia on the elements to be included in the employment services in TVET, (2) Development of the Manual on employment services in TVET; (3) Training of TVET directors and key persons on the use of the Manual; (4) Pilot the implementation of the employment services in TVET institution; and (5) Finalize the Manual and adoption of the Manual by the Minister of Labour and Vocational Training. With the support of the Ministry of Human Resource and Social Security/the government of China, the ILO/China project on &quot;Strengthening Skill Development in Cambodia, Lao, and Myanmar through South-South and Triangular Cooperation&quot; has partnered with Shanghai Jie Da Decision Consulting, a private partner from Shanghai, to conduct the requirement assessment, programming development and donation of software and hardware in the collaboration for e-public employment services. ILO has provided technical input in the development of the modules and in organizing the online training. In addition, the ILO has also mobilized the target beneficiaries through the partnership with trade union.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.5.1. Number of member States with strengthened employment services to support transitions to decent work</narrative>
