    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output A.1. More accurate and sustainable statistics on decent work using the latest statistical standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The public and private employment services benefit from the findings of the &quot;Rapid Assessment of Emerging Needs for Workers and Skills in Times of COVID-19 Crisis&quot; conducted by the National Employment Agency (NEA), in order to enhance their employment services responding to the current market demand of the workers and skills in time of COVID-19. ILO, through ILO/SDC &quot;Decent Employment for Youth in Cambodia&quot; and ILO/Sida &quot;Increased capacity of constituents to formulate and implement gender-responsive national employment policies, identify skills mismatches and future skill needs&quot; projects supported the National Employment Agency (NEA) to conduct a &quot;Rapid Assessment of Emerging Needs for Workers and Skills in Times of COVID-19 Crisis&quot;, which aimed at aims at understanding the employment changes and skills needs during the COVID-19 crisis for a better insightful on the current labour market in order to support the operation of the public and private employment services.</narrative>
   </description>
